        "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux\" style=\"display:none\">Subfield of computer science and mathematics</div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1368532237\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">This article is about the branch of computer science and mathematics. For the journal, see <a href=\"/wiki/Theoretical_Computer_Science_(journal)\" title=\"Theoretical Computer Science (journal)\"><i>Theoretical Computer Science</i> (journal)</a>.</div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Not to be confused with <a href=\"/wiki/Theory_of_computation\" title=\"Theory of computation\">Theory of computation</a>.</div>\n<figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:DFAexample.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/DFAexample.svg/250px-DFAexample.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/DFAexample.svg/500px-DFAexample.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"500\" data-file-height=\"299\" /></a><figcaption>A <a href=\"/wiki/Finite-state_automaton\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Finite-state automaton\">finite-state automaton</a> from <a href=\"/wiki/Automata_theory\" title=\"Automata theory\">automata theory</a>, a branch of theoretical computer science</figcaption></figure>\n<p><b>Theoretical computer science</b> is a subfield of <a href=\"/wiki/Computer_science\" title=\"Computer science\">computer science</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a> that focuses on the <a href=\"/wiki/Abstraction\" title=\"Abstraction\">abstract</a> and mathematical foundations of <a href=\"/wiki/Computation\" title=\"Computation\">computation</a>.\n</p><p>It is difficult to circumscribe the theoretical areas precisely. The <a href=\"/wiki/Association_for_Computing_Machinery\" title=\"Association for Computing Machinery\">ACM</a>'s <a href=\"/wiki/Special_Interest_Group_on_Algorithms_and_Computation_Theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Special Interest Group on Algorithms and Computation Theory\">Special Interest Group on Algorithms and Computation Theory</a> (SIGACT) provides the following description:<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1244412712\">.mw-parser-output .templatequote{overflow:hidden;margin:1em 0;padding:0 32px}.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{line-height:1.5em;text-align:left;margin-top:0}@media(min-width:500px){.mw-parser-output .templatequotecite{padding-left:1.6em}}</style><blockquote class=\"templatequote\"><p>TCS covers a wide variety of topics including <a href=\"/wiki/Algorithms\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Algorithms\">algorithms</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Data_structure\" title=\"Data structure\">data structures</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Computational_complexity_theory\" title=\"Computational complexity theory\">computational complexity</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Parallel_computation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Parallel computation\">parallel</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Distributed_computation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Distributed computation\">distributed</a> computation, <a href=\"/wiki/Probabilistic_computation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Probabilistic computation\">probabilistic computation</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Quantum_computation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quantum computation\">quantum computation</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Automata_theory\" title=\"Automata theory\">automata theory</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Information_theory\" title=\"Information theory\">information theory</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Cryptography\" title=\"Cryptography\">cryptography</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Program_semantics\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Program semantics\">program semantics</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Formal_methods\" title=\"Formal methods\">verification</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Algorithmic_game_theory\" title=\"Algorithmic game theory\">algorithmic game theory</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\">machine learning</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Computational_biology\" title=\"Computational biology\">computational biology</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Computational_economics\" title=\"Computational economics\">computational economics</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Computational_geometry\" title=\"Computational geometry\">computational geometry</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Computational_number_theory\" title=\"Computational number theory\">computational number theory</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Symbolic_computation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Symbolic computation\">algebra</a>. Work in this field is often distinguished by its emphasis on mathematical technique and <a href=\"/wiki/Rigor#Mathematical_rigour\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rigor\">rigor</a>.</p></blockquote>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\">.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .